# 🤖 LangGraph + Streamlit AI Chatbot

A simple AI chatbot built using **LangGraph**, **Groq Llama 3.3 70B**, and **Streamlit**. The chatbot supports real-time streaming responses, conversation memory, and multiple chat threads.

---

## Features Completed

### ✅ LangGraph Backend
- Created a `StateGraph`
- Defined the `ChatState`
- Added a chat node
- Connected `START → chat_node → END`
- Compiled the graph using `InMemorySaver`

---

### ✅ Groq Integration
- Loaded the Groq API key from the `.env` file
- Connected the chatbot with the Groq Llama 3.3 70B model
- Generated AI responses using LangGraph

---

### ✅ Streamlit Interface
- Built a clean chatbot UI
- Added a chat input box
- Displayed user and assistant messages
- Used Streamlit chat components

---

### ✅ Chat History
- Stored conversation history using `st.session_state`
- Reloaded previous messages whenever the app reruns

---

### ✅ LangGraph Integration
- Sent user messages to LangGraph
- Received AI responses
- Displayed responses in the Streamlit interface

---

### ✅ Streaming Responses
- Used `chatbot.stream()`
- Displayed responses using `st.write_stream()`
- AI responses are shown word by word for a better user experience

---

### ✅ Thread Support
- Used LangGraph thread IDs
- Each conversation runs in its own thread
- Makes conversation memory independent for every chat

